      },
      "message": "fix(heights): model-referenced heights read the setup's parts, never its fixtures\n\nTop of Model and Bottom of Model resolved through solid_aabb_in, which\nwalks every model - vises, accessories, plates and tagged fixtures of\nany setup included. A default contour in a document with a vise ran\ndown to the vise base and generate said ok.\n\nBoth references (and their \"no model loaded\" diagnostic) now read\nsetup_align::part_aabb_in: every non-fixture model in the asking\nsetup's frame. solid_aabb_in, is_model and the collision laws are\nunchanged, so verify still strikes a pass into the vise.\n\nPinned by tests/heights_fixtures.rs (five tests, mutation-checked).\n\nFixes #1529\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
